1. Definitions

1.1. "Licensor" means each copyright holder, or a party authorized by that
holder, who applies this License to material identified in a copyright notice,
file header, or project license notice. Each Licensor grants rights only to
the extent that they have authority to do so.

1.2. "Software" means the source code, object code, documentation,
configuration, and other copyrightable material identified as covered by this
License. Separately identified third-party materials retain their own terms.

1.3. "Covered Work" means the Software and the parts of any modified or combined
work that incorporate or are derived from copyrightable material in the
Software. An independent component does not become part of a Covered Work
solely because it is distributed alongside that work, used with it, or
communicates with it through an API or standard interface.

1.4. "Direct Variant" means a packaged or hosted version of the Software or a
modified Covered Work offered as a version of the Software or whose principal
practical function is supplied by the Software or material derived from it.
Renaming, repackaging, changing the interface, adding optional services, or
including minor ancillary features does not by itself change this
classification. A product with substantial independent functionality that
includes a Covered Work as one feature may qualify for Section 3.3.

1.5. "Covered Functionality" means functionality as implemented by a Covered
Work. It does not include a similar function independently implemented without
using protected expression from the Software.

1.6. "Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for modifying the exact
Covered Work distributed or operated, including its modifications, interface
definitions specific to it, and scripts, configurations, and instructions
reasonably necessary to build, install, and run it. It excludes independent
components outside the Covered Work, unmodified general-purpose tools and system
libraries, private credentials, and personal data. Provide usable example
settings or instructions where credentials or private configuration would
otherwise be needed.

1.7. "Distribute" means to convey a copy to another person or legal entity,
including by providing a download. Operation of a service without conveying a
copy is addressed in Section 5.

1.8. "Contributor" means a person or entity who intentionally submits
copyrightable material for inclusion and authorizes its inclusion under this
License.

2. Copyright Permission

Subject to the terms of this License, each Licensor grants you a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free copyright license, perpetual subject to
Section 10, to use, run, study, reproduce, modify, and Distribute the Software
and to create, use, and Distribute modified and combined works. This grant
includes private, educational, research, organizational, and commercial use.

3. Commercial Use and Charging

3.1. Commercial use is permitted. You may use the Software for internal
operations, development, testing, research, or business infrastructure and
receive revenue from your independent activities, subject to Sections 3.2–3.4.

3.2. Free distribution of the Software and Direct Variants. You must not require
payment or a purchase to obtain a copy of the Software or a Direct Variant that
you Distribute, or to install, activate, or use its Covered Functionality.
The same rule applies when you offer a Direct Variant as a hosted service.
Charging through a mandatory bundle, installation fee, account fee,
subscription, or intermediary is subject to the same rule. Availability of a
free copy elsewhere does not permit charging for a copy you Distribute under
this License.

3.3. Integration into an independent paid product. You may include a Covered
Work in a product or service with substantial independent functionality and
charge for that product or service if all the following conditions apply.

(a) The price is independently supportable by the product's independent
features or services. You must not add or increase a charge attributable to
access to or use of Covered Functionality. A generally applicable price
adjustment based on independent features, costs, or other reasons unrelated
to Covered Functionality is permitted.

(b) You must not require a separate purchase, paid add-on, activation fee,
additional usage charge, or move to a higher plan to obtain the Covered
Functionality. An existing paid product may include the functionality at its
existing price and in its existing relevant plans. A newly launched product
must be able to support its price and plan boundaries based on the
independent features or services offered.

(c) A higher plan may charge for substantially independent benefits. It may
include Covered Functionality provided at substantially equivalent terms in
the product's ordinary relevant plan, without an upgrade or separate purchase
for that functionality.

3.4. Advertising, sponsorship, voluntary donations, and optional fees for
genuine independent services such as support, customization, and general-purpose
hosting are permitted. Customers must be able to obtain and use any Software
or Direct Variant you Distribute without purchasing those services. In an
independent paid product, fees for hosting or support must be based on the
service supplied and must not be a condition imposed specifically on access
to Covered Functionality. A label such as "support" or "hosting" does not
authorize a disguised charge under Sections 3.2 or 3.3.

3.5. Nothing in this License restricts independent development, sale of a
competing implementation that does not use protected expression from the
Software, or use permitted without relying on this License.

4. Corresponding Source on Distribution

4.1. When you Distribute a Covered Work, provide its complete Corresponding
Source to each recipient at no additional charge. This requirement applies
to modified and unmodified covered binaries. Distributing complete
Corresponding Source with the copy satisfies this requirement.

4.2. You may provide Corresponding Source with the copy or give the recipient
a stable download link or written offer with practical instructions at the
time of distribution. If you use a link or written offer, keep the exact
version accessible to recipients free of additional charge for at least three
years after you last Distribute that version. You may provide the source
directly to recipients instead of making it publicly available. Recipients may
exercise their rights to the covered source under this License.

4.3. License the Covered Work, including your changes to it, under this
License when Distributing it. You may separately license independent material
outside the Covered Work. The source obligations extend to material that
incorporates or is derived from the Software, including the covered portions
of a combined work. Placing those portions in another file, repository,
package, or intermediary does not remove the obligation.

5. Modified Network Services

If you let users outside your legal entity interact remotely with a modified
Covered Work, including through an API or integrated frontend, offer those
users the complete Corresponding Source of the exact deployed Covered Work and
apply this License to its covered portions. Make the offer prominent,
accessible without a separate fee, and available for as long as you provide
access to that version. Independent services and components outside the
Covered Work remain outside this obligation.

Use restricted to people working on behalf of the same legal entity, solely
for that entity's internal operations and with no access for their own or
external purposes, does not trigger this section. Merely using an unmodified
Covered Work to provide a network service does not trigger the source duty in
this section. Section 4 applies whenever a copy is Distributed. Section 3
continues to apply to covered uses.

6. Notices and Attribution

When you Distribute a Covered Work or make it available under Section 5,
retain applicable copyright, attribution, and license notices. Include this
License or a durable link to its exact text. Identify the upstream project by
its stated name and canonical repository or project URL, if supplied. Place
that credit in a README, an About or notices screen, or documentation
provided with the work or service. Where reasonably practicable, identify
material changes and their dates. Do not imply authorship, endorsement, or
affiliation that does not exist.

7. Downstream Rights and Other Terms

Each recipient receives a license to the Covered Work from its respective
Licensors under these terms. You must not apply additional restrictions to
their exercise of rights in the Covered Work. You may license independent
material and offer separately authorized rights without reducing the rights
recipients already have under this License. Nothing here changes a separate
license validly granted for the same material or a previously released
version. If a third-party license prevents compliance with both sets of terms,
this License does not authorize Distribution of that combination.

8. Patents

To the extent they have authority to do so, each Licensor and Contributor
grants recipients a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free patent license
under claims they own or control that are necessarily infringed by their
contribution alone or by that contribution combined with the Software as
submitted. This applies to making, having made, using, offering to sell,
selling, importing, and otherwise transferring the covered implementation,
subject to the terms of this License.

If you institute patent litigation alleging that the Software or an
incorporated contribution constitutes direct or contributory patent
infringement, the patent licenses granted to you under this section terminate
when that litigation is filed, to the extent permitted by applicable law.

9. Trademarks

This License permits reasonable use of project names and marks to identify
origin and comply with Section 6. Any other trademark use requires separate
authorization where applicable.

10. Termination and Reinstatement

Your rights under this License terminate automatically if you materially
violate its terms. When you cease the violation, your rights from a particular
Licensor are provisionally reinstated. They become permanent unless that
Licensor notifies you of the violation within 60 days after you cease it.

If a Licensor notifies you of a violation and it is the first such notice you
have received from that Licensor for this Covered Work, your rights from that
Licensor are permanently reinstated when you cure the violation within 30 days
of receiving that notice. A termination of your rights does not by itself
terminate the rights of downstream recipients who continue to comply.

